+        "message": "We sincerely thank everyone who has taken the time to visit Tokyo International Theological Seminary. Our seminary follows the tradition of Reformed theology based on the Bible and is dedicated to training pastors and missionaries. Although Japan marks the 167th anniversary of Protestant missions, the current rate of evangelization remains below 1%. From a missiological perspective, Japan can truly be described as an \"unreached people group.\" Furthermore, it is deeply regrettable that within the Japanese Christian community today, the number of pastorless churches is increasing due to the aging of pastors, and churches with fewer than fifteen members that are not self-supporting now account for approximately 80% of all churches. Tokyo International Theological Seminary faces these realities of our time and seeks to play a role in bringing about transformation. By training pastors and missionaries who are fully equipped with the gospel of Jesus Christ’s atoning sacrifice on the cross and His resurrection, we are committed to igniting the vitality of life in the churches of Japan and throughout the nations. We humbly ask for your warm interest and prayers.",
